Comment: 
"// @@@ If the index is valid, within the list's bounds, and the role is not null, then for every position greater than the index and within the list's bounds, either the element at that position is null and was null before, or it remains unchanged from its previous state."

We are in method set(int index, Role role). Preconditions: index valid (within bounds), role not null. Postcondition: For every position j > index and within bounds, either element at j is null and was null before, or it remains unchanged from its previous state.

We need to use observers: contains(Role), get(int), size(), isEmpty() maybe. We have get method returning Role. We can compare old and new values. Use \old(this.get(j)). Also need to assert that if index is valid and role != null then condition holds. Use implication.

Define valid index: 0 <= index && index < this.size()? Since set replaces element at index, list must have that index already. In Java ArrayList, set index must be >=0 && < size. So condition: 0 <= index && index < this.size() && role != null. Then assert for all int j; j > index && j < this.size(); ( (this.get(j) == null && \old(this.get(j)) == null) || this.get(j).equals(\old(this.get(j))) ). But need to handle null equality. Use (this.get(j) == null && \old(this.get(j)) == null) || (this.get(j) != null && this.get(j).equals(\old(this.get(j)))) . Simpler: this.get(j) == \old(this.get(j)) or (this.get(j) != null && this.get(j).equals(\old(this.get(j)))) but equality for objects: we can use .equals. Use (this.get(j) == null ? \old(this.get(j)) == null : this.get(j).equals(\old(this.get(j)))) . But spec may allow using .equals when not null. Many examples used .equals directly, assuming non-null. They used this.query(i).equals(\old(this.query(i))). That assumes query returns non-null? In our case role may be null. So we need to handle null case.

We can express: (this.get(j) == null && \old(this.get(j)) == null) || this.get(j).equals(\old(this.get(j))) . That's fine.

Thus final assert:

assert (0 <= index && index < this.size() && role != null) => \forall int j; j > index && j < this.size(); ( (this.get(j) == null && \old(this.get(j)) == null) || this.get(j).equals(\old(this.get(j))) );

Make sure parentheses for implication: (0 <= index && index < this.size() && role != null) => \forall int j; j>index && j<this.size(); ( (this.get(j) == null && \old(this.get(j)) == null) || this.get(j).equals(\old(this.get(j))) );

